[{:seon.task/name "source-at-the-repl"
  :seon.task/plan "Agents read code the way a Clojure REPL does, and on Jolt that fails. Mined from T5 real run 3 (t5/out/real3.store, 2026-10-20): 4 of 8 agents evaluated (clojure.repl/source f), (clojure.repl/source-fn 'ns/f) or (require '[clojure.repl :refer [source]]) 171 times (\"No such var: clojure.repl/source\", \"source does not exist\"), and 3 agents tried (slurp (clojure.java.io/resource \"t5/forgive_test.clj\")) 53 times (\"Cannot open <nil> as a Reader\"): program code lives as facts (:var/src, :ns/src), not files. R4's run hit the same (20 times). What would a plain Clojure REPL do? `source` prints the definition and `source-fn` answers its text. In an agent, clojure.repl/source-fn and source answer a var's exact recorded text from the branch's db (seon.context/source-of), and doc works as at any REPL. Estimate: one AVET seek per call (seon.db/eid's cost)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.repl-test/source-answers-a-program-definition-from-its-facts}}
 {:seon.task/name "eval-record-keeps-a-failing-form-whole"
  :seon.task/plan "An eval record's :form is the form printed under the :form budget (600 tokens), so a failing form is cut (…N): mining T5 real run 3 could not read the whole defn that failed in t5.refusal/describe (it had to be recovered from the model's reply). Record the exact text the agent sent for a form that errs (N1 already cuts exact text from the reader's positions for defs: :var/src), bounded only by the request itself; a form that succeeds keeps its printed echo. Cost follows the failing forms only."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.repl-test/a-failing-form-is-recorded-whole}}
 {:seon.task/name "source-reads-the-program"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by the first DeepSeek agent on Seon's own code (2026-10-21, `seon.reconcile/a-refused-spawn-is-recorded`, 8 turns spent exploring, no fix written): `(clojure.repl/source seon.reconcile/stuck)` and the same for `advance`, `write`, `cas-tx`, `index` error in an agent's REPL (IllegalArgumentException or ExceptionInfo), because a compiled platform var has no source file the agent process can read. The program facts hold every form's exact text (`:form/src`, imported by `seon.source`; `seon.context/source-of` already reads it). An agent's REPL is a real Clojure REPL (AGENTS.md: get out of an agent's way), so `source` and `clojure.repl/source-fn` answer a var's recorded form text from the agent's branch db (its own redefinition if it made one), the way `doc` does, for platform and program vars alike. One reader: reuse `seon.context/source-of`, no second lookup."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.repl-test/source-answers-a-platform-var-from-the-program}}
 {:seon.task/name "an-eval-error-never-ends-the-attempt"
  :seon.task/plan "Measured 2026-10-22 06:4x on the standing root: attempt `seon.root/a-proc-answers-every-request-it-took#1` ended `:closed :error`, turns 0, reason \"seon.turn/work! threw: No matching field found: exists for class java.lang.String\", error `{:seon.error/type :seon.agent/eval-error :seon.error/operation seon.repl/eval-code :class IllegalArgumentException}`; its branch shows it re-evaluated every form of `my.root` (the ns form and each defn, unchanged text), most likely by `(require 'my.root :reload)` or `load-file` through lane RELOAD's loader hook (deleted 2026-10-22: a load now records nothing; the escape from `seon.repl/eval-code` may stand). An evaluation error is the agent's to read (a reply item with :tag :err), never the end of its attempt; this one escaped `seon.repl/eval-code` into `seon.turn/work!`, and the turn was not recorded, so the form that raised it is lost. A plain `(load-file \"src/my/root.clj\")` and `(require 'my.root :reload)` in a fresh agent answer nil (not reproduced). Correct: find the form and path that raise it (reload my.root after the agent's other turn-0 forms; a load whose form calls a File method on a path string), make every error raised while a loaded file's forms evaluate reach the agent as that load's :err item (Clojure's: the require throws, the REPL prints it), and record the turn before anything after the evaluation can fail. Proof: the reproducing forms in an agent answer an :err item and the agent takes its next turn."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.repl-test/an-error-inside-a-loaded-file-is-the-loads-error-item}}
 {:seon.task/name "one-item-shape-for-an-eval"
  :seon.task/plan "Shrink research row 30 (2026-10-22), dropped by root in brief 4: `seon.repl/record-tx` stores a reply item's :printed as :shown and :err as :error, so `seon.render.ui/eval-out` reads (or :printed :shown). Storing the item's own keys saves about 3 lines, but records are history and kept, so the old records would still need :shown read beside :printed forever: a permanent dual reader, the fallback AGENTS §9 names. Not worth it as a rename alone. Revisit only with a migration of the stored :seon.cluster.eval/record values that the owner approves (records are facts and kept), so one reader remains."
  :seon.task/kind :work}]
